{"title":"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 23","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An artist has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> cubes, each with an edge of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> meter.  She stands them on the ground to form a sculpture as shown.  She then paints the exposed surface of the sculpture.  How many square meters does she paint?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/4/714ffd00c9c6b2fd6f18b5ae9bc78a880fdc9fa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)}\\ 21 \\qquad \\text{(B)}\\ 24 \\qquad \\text{(C)}\\ 33 \\qquad \\text{(D)}\\ 37 \\qquad \\text{(E)}\\ 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"375\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/0/c907b9d8e0a7e2f4eb5dc0d61c0fe69439512738.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(2.35,-.15)--(2.44,.81)--(.09,.96)--cycle); draw((.783333333,-.05)--(.873333333,.91)--(1.135,1.135)); draw((1.566666667,-.1)--(1.656666667,.86)--(1.89,1.1)); draw((2.35,-.15)--(4.3,1.5)--(4.39,2.46)--(2.44,.81)); draw((3,.4)--(3.09,1.36)--(2.61,1.4)); draw((3.65,.95)--(3.74,1.91)--(3.29,1.94)); draw((.09,.96)--(.76,1.49)--(.71,1.17)--(2.2,1.1)--(3.6,2.2)--(3.62,2.52)--(4.39,2.46)); draw((.76,1.49)--(.82,1.96)--(2.28,1.89)--(2.2,1.1)); draw((2.28,1.89)--(3.68,2.99)--(3.62,2.52)); draw((1.455,1.135)--(1.55,1.925)--(1.89,2.26)); draw((2.5,2.48)--(2.98,2.44)--(2.9,1.65)); draw((.82,1.96)--(1.55,2.6)--(1.51,2.3)--(2.2,2.26)--(2.9,2.8)--(2.93,3.05)--(3.68,2.99)); draw((1.55,2.6)--(1.59,3.09)--(2.28,3.05)--(2.2,2.26)); draw((2.28,3.05)--(2.98,3.59)--(2.93,3.05)); draw((1.59,3.09)--(2.29,3.63)--(2.98,3.59)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"218\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The top view of this figure forms a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/2/39271c2314888f2dd21e70e67e9959a78bacae5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\text{ m} \\times 3\\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" /> square, so it has area <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/f/fefdf5e581303ff67fd537e1fd9ec6a005009e94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9\\text{ m}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>The left, right, front, and rear views each consist of six <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9eb8df3e19ae8d771c505ea2c78d43516231d619.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\text{ m} \\times 1\\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" /> squares stacked in a pyramid shape, so each of these views has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73e2b48bea5c44e6cc59bd48548e08f56c94280.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6\\text{ m}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"17\" />.  So, these views have a total area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/1/23153ed03393a511824b8be43ef4479824ecda4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\cdot 6 = 24 \\text{ m}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, the total painted area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/5162287e7d43a5a9f789fec6d4bd781254fa08d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + 24 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}\\ 33} \\text{ m}^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"166\" height=\"30\" />.  Note that the bottom is not painted.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_23&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME\" title=\"1989 AJHSME\">1989 AJHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=1989\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 22\">Problem 22</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1989_AJHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1989 AJHSME Proble